{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/670462-creating-a-setting-story-and-not-trying-to-offend","id":670462,"title":"Creating a Setting / Story and not trying to Offend...","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","Scion"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-09-18T21:36:31-07:00","id":670462,"title":"Creating a Setting / Story and not trying to Offend...","content":"So I have a setting in mind based primarily on medieval Japan with some hints of classical Japan.<br /> I had thought to base the main antagonistic force off of an Ainu Kamuy Yushkep (or perhaps Pauchi)with maybe a lovecraftian touch here and there.<br /> Then it occurs to me that while this story would probably only have a western audience, would it be poor form of me to go this route considering that the Ainu are still a discriminated against people group in Japan?<br /> Or am I over thinking things?<br /> <br /> <br /> Bit of a correction: When I put down Yushkep, I meant to put down Poronitne.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":490,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/490-omenseer","user":"omenseer","date":".  Correcting myself 09-19-2015, 11:59 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/490-omenseer","name":"omenseer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar490_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"987"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-18T21:57:54-07:00","id":670479,"title":"","content":"The thing about Scion is that virtually all of these pantheons were xenophobic at the time of their rule and discrimination was a pretty common and socially acceptable thing back then. So in the theme of the story, it would be expected. Besides, these games appear to be designed towards mature players, not young kids. So hopefully you're in a group who knows how to handle the situation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-19T00:04:01-07:00","id":670520,"title":"","content":"The fact that you are worried this might be a problem is an indication that this is probably not a problem. If you're the kind of person who worries about authenticity, being respectful of a culture that has faced harsh situations in the past and present, and the accidental social effects of lax messaging, then you're probably the kind of person who is going to do a little research and not be crass with your presentation.<br /> <br /> It's fiction using a real-world cultural basis as inspiration. As long as you treat Ainu characters as people, get a sense of what the myth is and where you're diverging from it, and avoid gross distortions with nasty implications like making all the religious Ainu universally dupes of horrible titans, you're golden, have fun, your game idea sounds neat.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-19T08:44:42-07:00","id":670994,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Stupid Loserman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/670462-creating-a-setting-story-and-not-trying-to-offend?p=670520#post670520\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The fact that you are worried this might be a problem is an indication that this is probably not a problem. If you're the kind of person who worries about authenticity, being respectful of a culture that has faced harsh situations in the past and present, and the accidental social effects of lax messaging, then you're probably the kind of person who is going to do a little research and not be crass with your presentation..</div> </div> </div> </div>100% agreed on this.<br /> <br /> One way I saw an attempt to split the difference was to create the situation you want and juxtapose it to a version of the disadvantaged culture you feel is more sympathetic to their plight. The situation was a Delta Green adventure for Call of Cthulhu where there was an &quot;Innsmoth situation, where an island in British Columbia was a Deep One/human symbiotic breeding community. They based the culture of the island on the Haida, but these pretty awful guys weren't supposed to represent the Haida as a whole. They were a part of the Haida that had gone a very very bad direction. The rest of the Haida were wary of them and they were associated with some aspects of Haida mythology that weren't so nice, but they were good enough at presenting a slightly slimy (pun intended) but borderline acceptable front. Kinda like a colony of Loki worshipers or Eris worshipers or Aghori (who you suspect are or may be harboring/fronting for thugges but don't have enough evidence to act on and, besides, they are kinda scarey....), Etc. <br /> <br /> It doesn't rise to the level of an elegant solution, in fact, there are many ways that it is still very problematic, but, with a sidebar about they fact they knew what they were doing and asked for the indulgence/apologized if offense was taken, it seems workable. Of course, some people are very sensitive and will be offended even so, so, check with your players (and yourself) to see if this covers your bases.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-19T09:01:02-07:00","id":671003,"title":"","content":"Thanks everyone. That sounds very solid.<br /> <br /> My plans for the Ainu in setting was to have them be opposed to imperial authority, but later convinced to join the fight.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/490-omenseer","name":"omenseer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar490_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"987"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}